  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
        <para id="para-00001"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_7_2_1_WU_27"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00015">Building Character: Proactivity</para>
<media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_02_02.png" height="200"/>
          </media>

            <para id="para-00016">Proactivity is the ability to take initiative. There’s evidence that proactivity is one of the qualities that distinguished the greatest American presidents from their peers.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Think about your current sense of proactivity. Are the following statements true for you??</para>
            <list id="list-00001">
          <item> I am always looking for better ways of doing things. </item>
          <item> I love to challenge the status quo. </item>
        </list>
            <para id="para-00018">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
